{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Write-path trace: a second foreign load, independent of the mount\n\nA `comment` from the same worktree with `.tickets-tracker` already symlinked also loaded the main checkout's config. Stack:\n`append_event -> write_and_push -> push_tickets_branch -> _push_mode -> resolve_push_mode -> load_config(root=/Users/joeoakhart/rebar)`.\n\nCause: `src/rebar/_store/push.py` `push_tickets_branch` calls `_push_mode(os.path.dirname(base_path))`. `base_path` is the resolved store path (`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker`), so its parent is the main checkout, and **every ticket write from a linked worktree takes `sync.push` from the main checkout's config**. Origin: 1d2d7983ca6 (2026-06-16), which passed an explicit root to avoid a git subprocess.\n\nPrior intent covers this site: auspicial-friended-merganser and scathing-custommade-bobcat (98f21fbcd86, e340337445e) set the rule that config reads resolve the caller's repo root, \"NOT os.path.dirname(tracker)\", at `_lib_gates.py`, `_cli/_execute.py`, `compact_trigger.py`, `validate.py`. `push.py` was not migrated. Neither `rebar.toml` on this host sets `[sync]`, so today the effect is the warning, not a different push mode.\n\nSo there are 2 sites:\n1. `_store/push.py` dirname(tracker) config root — prior rule settles the fix.\n2. `_commands/init.py` `_main_worktree_tracker` — reads the main checkout's config on purpose (3e28-f913-d06b-471a) to locate the main store; whether that read should validate/warn on the rest of the main config has no recorded intent. Escalated for a decision before claiming."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793532852847401001,"uuid":"1f531bd1-1e46-4275-b1da-85166833fa1c"}